  -> RUNG (causality, checked not assumed): at separation 48 the light cone (r*sweeps = 44 sites) cannot connect the injections within the run, so the interaction must be zero. Measured -0.0156 +/- 0.0096. Consistent with zero, so the comparison is measuring dynamics rather than harness error. PRIMARY: at separations where the cones meet, interaction is d=6: -2.5156±0.5633, d=12: -1.1719±0.2847, d=24: -0.5078±0.1262. Non-zero beyond 2 SE at separations [6, 12, 24], so two damage sites do NOT superpose: the lattice adds an interaction the local response does not have (F114 measured sub-additivity of +0.003 to +0.028, essentially additive). The sign is negative — INTERFERENCE: the pair damages LESS than the union of the singles, consistent with competition for the same sites or shared healing. BOUNDARY: one family, one radius, one temperature, plateau checkpoints only -- chosen because damage must reliably ignite for a superposition test to be defined at all, which excludes the dip where ignition is 0.05-0.3 (F42).

